WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.690
- [Narrator] With a head of
hair that can literally stun,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.632
this is the curly hair tarantula.

00:00:05.632 --> 00:00:08.215
(gentle music)

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.310
The unusual hairs on the
curly hair tarantula are

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.853
both its most distinguishing
feature and its best weapon.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.840
When threatened, it will
kick hairs off its abdomen

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.510
that blind looming predators.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.580
Found throughout Central
America, this burrowing species

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.680
is found in scrubland.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.620
Nocturnal by nature, the
curly hair tarantula is an

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.333
opportunistic hunter, ready
to eat whatever passes by.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.150
This spider has extremely
poor eyesight, but at the end

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.200
of its legs are receptors
that are sensitive to smell,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.500
taste and vibration.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.390
Once the tarantula detects
its prey, it injects

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.463
paralyzing venom through
two hollowed fangs.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:56.270
Despite their popularity
in the insect pet trade,

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.390
wild curly hair tarantulas
are at risk due to habitat

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.820
loss in Central America.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.562
This is the curly hair tarantula.

00:01:04.562 --> 00:01:07.145
(gentle music)

